    "durationMs": 318212,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. Summary of what I built in `/workspace`:\n\n**Implementation**\n- Rails 8 API-only app (`rails new . --api`) with PostgreSQL via `pg` 1.7, all deps installed up front.\n- `Link` model: `url` validated as an absolute http/https URI with a host; `code` validated against `\\A[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}\\z` and unique; codes auto-generated (`SecureRandom.alphanumeric(7)`) when omitted/blank; `clicks` bigint defaulting to 0.\n- `LinksController`: `create` (201 with `{code, url, clicks: 0}`, URL stored/echoed unchanged, 409 on duplicate custom code, 422 with `error` on validation failures, retry loop for the rare generated-code collision), `show` (200/404 JSON), `index` (`{items, total}` ordered by ascending id), and `resolve` for `GET /r/:code` (302 with exact `Location`, one atomic `clicks = clicks + 1` per request via `increment!`).\n- Malformed JSON (any content type), missing/invalid URL, and invalid codes all return 422 JSON with an `error` field; unmatched paths fall through to a JSON 404.\n- `config/database.yml` reads everything from `DATABASE_URL` (no hard-coded credentials); production config serves plain HTTP (`force_ssl`/`assume_ssl` disabled).\n- `start.sh`: sets production env + ephemeral `SECRET_KEY_BASE`, runs `bin/rails db:prepare` (creates/applies migrations), then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`. README documents startup.\n\n**Verification (all passed)**\n- 64 curl checks covering every endpoint, status code, JSON shape, charset boundaries (4/20-char codes, bad chars, unicode), malformed/partial/no-body inputs, and list ordering.\n- Concurrency: 20 parallel redirects yielded exactly +20 clicks; 10 parallel creates produced 10 unique codes.\n- Restart test via `sh start.sh`: all links and click counts survived; `db:prepare` re-runs as a no-op.\n\nServer and test processes are stopped, and the test data was wiped so the table starts empty."
